    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2D7qJNjFn3Rx8aSXYUXuWtE)_\n\n**Before:** seeing the output of one edit meant tangling all 130 module docs (the README block), or running `sp-tangle-all`, which listed four docs that no longer exist.\n\n**Reading of \"all notes\":** the literate module docs in `docs/tangles/` (tangled to `libraries/modules/`), not the `~/notes` vault.\n\n## Changes (`sp-org-babel` doc and module, README)\n- `sp-tangle-changed`: tangles only docs whose text changed since they were last tangled. It compares a SHA-1 of each doc with the one in `tangle-hashes.eld` in `sp-cache-dir`, written after a successful tangle. No git is needed, so it works with yadm and uncommitted edits. A doc is also tangled when it has no entry or an `.el` it wrote is missing. `C-u` forces all.\n- Changed `:tangle` path: the path is part of the doc text, so the doc is tangled to the new file; the old file is left in place and a message says so.\n- A failing doc is reported, keeps its old entry and is retried next time; deleted docs are dropped from the cache.\n- `sp-tangle-changed-and-reload`: also reloads the written modules that are loaded (via `sp-reload--run` if present, else `load`).\n- `sp-tangle-on-save-mode`: opt-in, tangles the saved doc if it changed.\n- `sp-tangle-all` now tangles every module doc; `sp-literate-files` is removed.\n- README: new \"Tangling only what changed\" section (Emacs and shell).\n\nNot done: a git-diff mode (the hash cache covers the same need without requiring commits).\n\n## Tested\nEmacs 29.3 in batch on the real tree: 130 docs found, first run tangled 167 files, second run 0. A scratch tree covered a retargeted doc, a deleted output, and force. Not run in the interactive config. A full tangle also rewrites ~20 modules that differ from their docs (final newline and similar); I did not commit those.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBo9meNfQTQJaUvhx2)_",
